# Build context is the repo root (docker build -f deploy/Dockerfile ., or wrangler with image_build_context = "..").
# Two copies, kept identical (deploy/tests/test_artifacts.py): deploy/Dockerfile.dockerignore, which BuildKit reads
# for `-f deploy/Dockerfile`, and /.dockerignore, which is the only one that applies to wrangler's build: wrangler
# pipes the Dockerfile in (`docker build -f - <repo>`), so there is no Dockerfile path to find the first one by.
# Papers and secrets never go into the image.
# index/ (the paper index, if present) does: deploy/start.py uses it when R2 or the /data volume has none.
.git
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/node_modules
**/.wrangler
.reference
papers
index/.*.tmp
**/.env
**/.env.*
!deploy/env.example
**/.dev.vars
deploy/.state
deploy/data
*.egg-info
build
# The page and the Worker are deployed by wrangler, not run by the backend. Keeping them out means a page edit
# doesn't change the image (and doesn't restart the container on the next deploy).
web
cloudflare
docs
.claude
